    "publishedAt": "2026-11-23",
    "summary": "But the FCC originally adopted its media ownership rules in the pre-Internet era. These long-overdue updates will put local broadcasters in a far better position to attract investment, serve the public interest, and strengthen the community reporting Americans rely on. But today's stations compete not only with one another, but also with an array of online competitors that did not exist when many of the current ownership restrictions were adopted. The Commission's proposal would update these rules for the modern marketplace, helping ensure that local broadcasters can continue investing in journalism, public safety, and service to their communities.",
