    "summary": "The expanded High-Performance Computing (HPC) infrastructure, developed through the collaboration between Ducati and Lenovo, added around 48% more processing power and roughly doubled the available memory, enabling the Ducati Lenovo Team to harness the power of technology to support Márquez’s championship bid. Lenovo workstations, edge servers, and HPC infrastructure provided the processing power, storage and connectivity to enable the team to rapidly process data, compare it with the rider’s perceptions and identify where changes could be made to improve performance within the narrow window between sessions. Lenovo technology has continued to help power the team’s innovation and performance throughout the year, while supporting its preparations for a new era of MotoGP.",
