    "publishedAt": "2026-11-12",
    "summary": "HOUSTON – November 12, 2026 – HPE today introduced two new supercomputing and rack-scale innovations to help customers improve storage economics and enhance cooling efficiencies. New hybrid configurations of HPE Cray Supercomputing Storage Systems E2000 create the world’s fastest hybrid supercomputing storage1, and the HPE Rack Management Controller improves cooling and power of high-density racks. More capacity, same data center footprint : Creating up to 32% more usable storage capacity per rack 4 , helping customers support growing datasets without expanding rack space. The integration shares rack-level telemetry and control capabilities, improving visibility and making it easier to operate and expand large, liquid-cooled HPC and AI environments.",
