    "publishedAt": "2026-11-02",
    "summary": "It can act within its permissions and still produce an unintended result. An AI agent can act within its permissions and still stop legitimate processes, so measure service outcomes, not just component health Every critical service needs a clear owner and clear limits on what agents can change on their own, what needs approval, and who can step in Consider a bank where an AI agent changes a fraud rule and legitimate payments stop going through. Assign accountability before disruption A service may span several teams, each responsible for a component. Measure service outcomes, not just system health Component health is not the same as service health.",
