    "publishedAt": "2026-11-17",
    "summary": "SpaceX and Qualcomm recently announced a multi-year supply agreement under which SpaceX will widely adopt Qualcomm’s Dragonwing 5G base station chipset solutions. TrendForce believes the partnership will significantly reduce SpaceX’s base station deployment costs while simplifying system integration across equipment from multiple vendors, thereby accelerating the large-scale commercial rollout of its 5G network. Pre-integrated O-RAN solutions help SpaceX reduce dependence on traditional equipment vendors TrendForce projects the global 5G infrastructure’s market value will reach US$55 billion in 2027, up 24.3% YoY, as 5G applications diversify, subscriber numbers rise, and 5G fixed wireless access (FWA) gains traction. Potential suppliers include Amphenol for base station antenna development and Qorvo for power amplifiers (PAs), while American Tower and Crown Castle could provide tower leasing and site infrastructure support.",
