    "summary": "If there was one humble component relatively safe from the component crisis brought about by the AI boom, it was the PCB. Companies in the automotive, industrial, defense, medical, and telecom sectors are reportedly struggling to secure enough supply. The industry is trying to expand to match the demand, with at least $10 billion going into PCB plants in Southeast Asia and China over the past three years. Last month, we reported that some PCB orders were taking up to 30 months , and motherboard prices also increased roughly 15% to 50%.",
