    "publishedAt": "2026-11-25",
    "summary": "Digital Realty acquired 3800 Golf Road (aka Atrium Corporate Center) in Rolling Meadows in September for $81.5 million. Per recent city documents, the company now aims to demolish the existing building and develop two two-story data center buildings totaling about 975,000 square feet (90,580 sqm) and 156MW of IT capacity, and a 240MW ComEd substation on a separate 4.6-acre lot. Private real estate investment firm Brennan Investment Group acquired the site in 2023, planning to demolish the site and construct a new 600,000 sq ft (55,741 sqm) industrial park known as Rolling Meadows Commerce Center or RMC². Spear Street Capital had previously acquired the site in 2010 for around $27m.",
