    "publishedAt": "2026-11-24",
    "summary": "Fan business serves data centers and other HVAC markets ABB plans to acquire cooling company Ziehl-Abegg for an enterprise value of $2.65 billion and an equity value of $2.22bn. Ziehl-Abegg manufactures axial, centrifugal, and process fans, internal and external rotor motors, ventilation systems, and integrated control systems for a number of market verticals, including data centers. The Künzelsau, Germany-based business is expected to generate approximately $1.4bn of revenue in 2026, with an operational EBITA margin in the mid-single-digit range. Together, we can create a more comprehensive offering of components for cooling and ventilation systems customers, helping us better address their needs, strengthen our position in attractive markets and support profitable growth.",
